# XSH gai_strerror()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.gai_strerror.001
anchor     functions/gai_strerror.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       For each of the ten error values the page lists, the return value is a pointer to a non-empty string.
note       The text of the string is implementation-defined, so only its presence is checked.
test       t/001-known-codes.c

assertion  XSH.gai_strerror.002
anchor     functions/gai_strerror.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       For a value that is none of the listed error values, the return value is a pointer to a non-empty string.
note       The page says the contents indicate an unknown error; no wording is fixed, so only presence is checked.
test       t/002-unknown-code.c
